  "title": "Simultaneous partition of hypergraphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem Let $H_1$ and $H_2$ be two $r$-uniform hypergraph on the same vertex set $V$. Does there always exist a partition of $V$ into $r$ classes $V_1, \\dots, V_r$ such that for both $i=1,2$, at least $r!m_i/r^r -o(m_i)$ hyperedges of $H_i$ meet each of the classes $V_1, \\dots, V_r$?",
